{"name":"Black Is Back","hex":"#0f1519","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"back","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At or near the rear.","Returned or restored to a previous place or condition."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["To or in a previous condition or place.","In a direction opposite to that in which someone or something is facing or normally pointing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/back"}],"entries":[{"title":"Human back","blocks":[{"text":"The human back, also called the dorsum, is the large posterior area of the human body, rising from the top of the buttocks to the back of the neck. It is the surface of the body opposite from the chest and the abdomen. The vertebral column runs the length of the back and creates a central area of recession. The breadth of the back is created by the shoulders at the top and the pelvis at the bottom."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_back"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Posterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APosterior_view_of_human_female_and_male_backs_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/120px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/250px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Gray204.png/120px-Gray204.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray204.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Back_Muscles.jpg/120px-Back_Muscles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Back_Muscles.jpg/250px-Back_Muscles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa